  "description": "REST request body. input.payload is the ordered list of [key, value] pairs (the wire key order is kept, never sorted). A value is a string, or a nested object or list of such values (the OCO bodies): an object's keys and a list's items keep the order the file gives them (in this file every object that is a value is written in wire order, not sorted), and the rules below apply to every string at any depth. The body is jData= followed by compact JSON (separators \",\" and \":\", no spaces), non-ASCII characters written as UTF-8 (no \\u escapes), no HTML escaping of < > & or ', then only % & + percent-encoded, in that order (% first). Everything else, including = space / ? #, is sent as is. JSON string escapes: \" and \\ as \\\" and \\\\; the control characters U+0008, U+0009, U+000A, U+000C, U+000D as \\b \\t \\n \\f \\r; every other character below U+0020 as \\u00XX with lower-case hex; DEL (U+007F), U+2028 and U+2029 are sent raw as UTF-8. expected.utf8_hex is the exact body bytes. A lone surrogate in any key or value at any depth cannot be encoded as UTF-8: nothing is sent and the call is {\"error\": \"RequestValidationError\", \"fields\": [...]}, fields being the sorted top-level keys that hold it (a nested value is named by its top-level key). Such an input is written in the file with its \\uXXXX escape.",
